 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Real Estate Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a real estate landing page?\", \"a\": \"A single page that asks one kind of visitor for one thing, such as a home address from an owner who wants a price opinion. A buyer page asks for a showing time instead. It carries one form and no site menu, and its headline matches the ad or yard sign that sent the visitor. Every lead it collects is meant for an agent to call.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I build a real estate agent landing page?\", \"a\": \"Pick one offer and one audience, then describe both in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>. Name the questions the form should ask and the agent who gets each lead. Emergent builds the page and the lead table, and any change after that is another message.\"}, {\"q\": \"What layout do the best real estate landing pages use?\", \"a\": \"A short one that fits a phone screen: a headline naming the offer, one photo, the agent's name, and the first question of the form. Anything that pushes the form below that first screen, like a photo carousel or a long bio, belongs further down the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find real estate landing page templates?\", \"a\": \"Leadpages and Framer both list templates for agents. A template gives you the layout and the form fields, and the question of who gets each lead stays open. With Emergent, the routing behind the form and a lead table you own come from the same prompt as the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good real estate landing page examples to study?\", \"a\": \"Dribbble keeps a tagged gallery of real estate landing page designs. Look past the photography to the form: how many fields it has, which question comes first, and what a visitor sees after submitting. The strongest pages ask a seller for the address before anything else.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an open house landing page include?\", \"a\": \"It needs the address, the open house hours, and a sign-in short enough to finish at the door. NAR's guidance says the host agent needs no written buyer agreement with visitors, though anyone who later tours with an agent signs one first. Send each sign-in to a thank you page with the listing sheet.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a cash buyers landing page?\", \"a\": \"It is the page an investor runs to buy houses for cash, usually from owners who want to sell as is. The form asks about repairs and timing. Like any <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/lead-generation-landing-page'>lead generation landing page</a>, it should state plainly who is buying and how offers are worked out.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many real estate landing pages should an agent build?\", \"a\": \"One for each offer and audience you advertise. That could mean a home value page per farm area, one page per active listing, and a single sign-in page reused at every open house. A page with no ad, sign, or mailer pointing at it collects few leads.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the benefits of landing pages for real estate?\", \"a\": \"They keep a visitor from an ad on one offer, with no listings menu or blog to wander into, and they launch faster than a full site. Each lead arrives tagged with its page, which shows which ad or sign is working. An agent who also wants a bio and a contact form can add a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/one-page-website'>one page website</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a realtor landing page free to build?\", \"a\": \"It can be. Some builders let you make and publish one on a free plan, while the ads and the CRM behind it are separate costs. Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing a page with a live URL.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}